from pathlib import Path
import json
P=Path(__file__).parent
DATA='''knot|The wrong size|You feel too small for your life because you measure yourself against everything that happens|What exactly is being measured: the body, a passing thought, or the awareness in which both are known?|Do not confuse the fact of being aware with an inflated claim that you are personally omnipotent|When the next small task arrives, do it at its actual scale
knot|The knot called mine|A familiar worry always returns carrying your name|Can you describe the worry as a thought with a beginning and an end rather than as the entirety of yourself?|The possessive 'mine' is a grammatical habit; a metaphysical claim about self requires further argument|Tell the truth about the worry and take any needed action
knot|A history mistaken for a self|Your biography seems to exhaust what you are|Who knows the story at this moment, and which details must be recalled for that knowing to occur?|Autobiography matters ethically and psychologically, but narrative memory does not function exactly like immediate awareness|Remember what matters without making the story a prison
knot|The desire for completion|You postpone life until a future spiritual state arrives|How would you know the promised state had come, and who would make that judgment?|The longing for an experience can become another object of attachment|Resume today's concrete obligation without cancelling the longer search
 given|The fact of appearing|Before you judge a sight, it is already given as experience|Can you find a sensation that appears to you without any appearing at all?|The question concerns the conditions of experience, not whether the physical world is mind-made|Describe what is present before interpreting it
 given|The certainty and its limits|You are more certain that you are experiencing than that your interpretation is correct|Which claim is immediate: that something is appearing, or why it appears?|Do not infer that every appearance is true; self-evidence of experience differs from certainty about objects|Correct your beliefs when better evidence arrives
 given|Attention does not create everything|Concentrating on an object seems to make it more real|What changes when attention turns away: the object's existence, or your present acquaintance with it?|Trika's emphasis on consciousness does not mean your private attention manufactures other people|Look back at the object and allow its independence to matter
 given|The missing second lamp|You seek another witness to prove the first act of knowing|If one act of knowing required a second knower, what would establish the second?|The regress of recognition invites a self-luminous account, but it is an argument, not a word trick|Notice an ordinary perception without demanding an inner spectator
 subject|The body as visible|You say 'I am my body' and then look at your hand|Is the body experienced as known, and does its being known settle what the subject is?|The body is indispensable to ordinary life; a distinction between knower and known is not contempt for embodiment|Care for the body that allows your life to continue
 subject|A thought can be noticed|A thought says 'this is who I am'|Does every thought that appears have to be the entire subject of appearing?|Witnessing language can help, but treating awareness as a hidden internal object creates a new problem|Let the thought finish before acting on it
 subject|The ache of agency|You cannot tell whether you really choose|Where in experience do you meet intention, action, hindsight and their differences?|Agency requires philosophical argument; immediate feeling cannot settle free will by itself|Own your next choice without inventing certainty about its metaphysics
 subject|The word I|The same pronoun attaches to child, adult, tired, joyful and grieving|What allows one word to serve across so many changing predicates?|Grammar reveals continuity of reference but not a proof of an eternal individual soul|Use the pronoun responsibly rather than worshipping it
 object|The cup on the table|An ordinary cup seems entirely outside the act of knowing|What in the description belongs to the cup, and what to your present experience of it?|Distinguish epistemic access from the cup's physical existence; recognition is not solipsism|Drink the water instead of trying to dissolve the cup
 object|Colour is relational|The same cloth looks different in noon and twilight|Does a change of appearance entail that no real cloth exists?|An appearance has conditions; an account of consciousness need not deny those conditions|Look again under better light when accuracy matters
 object|Difference without distance|You can distinguish a sound from a thought without making either unreal|Do differences in experience require absolute separation from the fact of awareness?|Nonduality must allow genuine distinctions rather than forcing every object into a vague sameness|Name what is different with care
 object|The world is not a private dream|Other people's pain refuses to behave like your chosen image|What keeps you from using metaphysics to minimise an other's reality?|The world may be interpreted as manifestation without excusing indifference or cruelty|Answer a person rather than a theory
 other|Another first person|You meet someone who also says 'I'|What changes when your account of experience must accommodate their own first-person life?|An expansive account of consciousness has to make room for more than one's private certainty|Listen long enough to discover an unexpected fact
 other|The argument|A disagreement feels like proof that the other is foreign to you|Can a shared situation contain genuine incompatible judgments?|Recognition should enlarge the space for disagreement, not dissolve it by declaration|State their position fairly before replying
 other|The obligation|You recognise a neighbour's need while busy with something important|Does identifying yourself as universal make you more or less accountable to this person?|Any spiritual insight that removes ordinary obligation needs severe scrutiny|Help if you can; otherwise answer truthfully
 other|The name offered back|A person's name is spoken with care|What is honoured when you use another's own chosen name?|Speech is relation in action; devotional metaphysics cannot replace basic courtesy|Say the name correctly and ask when uncertain
 energies|Wanting|Desire appears before you have formed a plan|Can you distinguish wanting, judging and acting, even when they arrive almost together?|The triad of will, knowledge and action is a philosophical framework for these differences|Choose whether to pursue the desire after considering consequences
 energies|Knowing|You perceive an object and then make a claim about it|What makes a perception sufficient or insufficient reason for a judgment?|Śakti as cognition is not a licence to call guesses revelation|Check the claim against evidence
 energies|Doing|A decision becomes a movement of the body|Which abilities and constraints made the action possible?|Action can be read as participation in a wider field, while responsibility remains particular|Finish the act you began or explicitly stop it
 energies|The three not three things|Wanting, understanding and acting can be separated in analysis|Are they independent substances or distinguishable functions within one situation?|The triad's nondual reading is not a denial that real action can fail|Correct the action when knowledge changes
 methods|A precise pause|You notice a gap between impulse and response|Does the gap require prolonged breath control or can it be noticed ordinarily?|Some traditional practices attend to intervals, but a modern pause must be named as a modern suggestion|Answer after checking what is actually being asked
 methods|The question who|You turn from object to the felt fact of knowing|Are you finding a second object called the witness?|An inner inquiry is a method only if its source, instructions and limits are identified|Return to the conversation you were in
 methods|The word and the hearing|You repeat a word until its sound becomes clear|Which aspects are phonetic, semantic and devotional?|Mantra practices vary; not every word is a consecrated mantra and not every phoneme implies a deity|Let pronunciation become accurate without making it a contest
 methods|Without a method|A moment of clarity comes while no practice is underway|Does its spontaneity prove that all preparation was useless?|Anupāya is a doctrinal category, not a universal excuse to abandon disciplines|Do not perform the clarity; continue normally
 signs|The danger of a sign|You wait for warmth, light or a sudden sensation|Why would any one bodily event be proof of liberation?|No reliable equation maps one sensation to ultimate spiritual success|Notice the sensation if it occurs and do not chase it
 signs|Fewer excuses|After reflection, an old excuse seems less persuasive|Does your conduct become more accountable or merely more self-congratulatory?|Changes in behaviour are worth noticing but are not metaphysical proof|Make one repair rather than announce progress
 signs|The return of confusion|You lose a clear feeling and conclude you have fallen|Was the clear feeling itself the truth, or one temporary condition?|Recognition cannot be reduced to the duration of an altered mood|Resume a reasonable routine
 signs|Compassion without display|A chance to help appears with no audience|Are you doing it because it is needed or because it confirms an identity?|Quiet action can be ethically valuable without needing sacred self-description|Do it if you can and move on
 ordinary|The breakfast bowl|Breakfast is exactly as it was yesterday|What has changed, if anything, in the way you meet a simple object?|A philosophy that cannot coexist with dishes and hunger has not yet reached ordinary life|Eat and wash the bowl
 ordinary|The unanswered message|Someone has not replied, and theories bloom|Can you distinguish actual evidence from a story produced by uncertainty?|Recognition doesn't exempt you from communication or the limits of knowing another|Write clearly if a reply is needed
 ordinary|The difficult apology|You understand your reasoning and still caused harm|Does insight erase the act or make acknowledgment more urgent?|A language of universal agency must never swallow particular responsibility|Apologise without metaphysical decoration
 ordinary|The road home|After a great journey the same street waits|What need be added to the world for the street to be encountered directly?|The ordinary is not a disappointing substitute for awakening; it is where every claim is tested|Unlock the door, greet the people inside, and stay'''
SECTIONS=['knot','given','subject','object','other','energies','methods','signs','ordinary']
records=[]
for line in DATA.splitlines():
 if not line.strip():continue
 bits=[x.strip() for x in line.split('|')]
 if len(bits)!=6:raise ValueError((len(bits),line[:60]))
 s,title,cost,q,analysis,return_=bits
 records.append({'id':f'rec-{len(records)+1:02d}','section':s,'title':title,'cost':cost,'question':q,'recognition':analysis,'return':return_,'source_unit':None,'proof_status':'OWNER_APPROVAL_REQUIRED','genre':'original_editorial_philosophical_primer'})
assert len(records)==36 and all(sum(x['section']==s for x in records)==4 for s in SECTIONS)
intro='''# RECOGNITION: A MANUAL — 36 COMPLETE ORIGINAL CANDIDATE SPREADS

**Status:** An original, fully written **English candidate primer** for the 36-slot design. This deliberately DOES NOT claim to reproduce Tantrasāra, Spanda or any other scripture. The old thesis bans agent-written connective prose; the owner must explicitly approve a new `original editorial primer` content contract before merging. Source-verified Sanskrit selections may be added later as optional quotations with provenance. The present book has no fake scriptural text.

## Proposed introduction

You can recognise an error in a sentence without finding a new object. You can discover that the person you were looking for has been in the room all along. Recognition is different from producing the person by thinking correctly. Nondual Śaiva philosophy applies a radical version of this idea to awareness and the world. It argues that what you take to be a separate, insufficient self is an appearance within a more fundamental consciousness.

This is not an empirical fact you must accept before turning the page. The following thirty-six short inquiries ask you to notice distinctions that philosophy can use and to see where it must still argue. They cannot replace a lineage's initiation, prove every metaphysical claim, or guarantee a permanent state. The work begins with what you can check now: how a thought appears, what you mean by “I,” and whether what is known exhausts knowing itself.

Each page contains an ordinary cost, a question, a careful recognitional distinction, and an action that returns the inquiry to life. When a page makes a bigger metaphysical claim than its observation entails, the difference must remain visible. This is a manual for accurate attention, not a certificate of enlightenment.

---
'''
md=intro
for i,x in enumerate(records,1):
 if i%4==1:md+=f"\n## {x['section'].title()}\n\n"
 md+=f'''### {i:02d}. {x['title']} [{x['id']}]
**The ordinary cost.** {x['cost']}.

**The inquiry.** {x['question']}

**The precise turn.** {x['recognition']}

**Return.** {x['return']}.

**Source status (editor only):** This is original synthesis. No exact Sanskrit source is asserted. Any future Trika quotation needs witness proof and separate attribution.

'''
md+='''## Final page: a complete ordinary act

No final exercise asks you to manufacture a state. The inquiry has come through thoughts, objects, other people, action and the hazards of measuring progress. Each time it returned to something concrete. If there is a recognition worth keeping, it will have to survive that return. The door opens onto the same street. Nothing in the street is required to know that you have read a book.

## Why the contract needs to change

The current thesis demands new, personally impactful explanatory prose and simultaneously forbids all agent-written connective prose. These 36 pieces are owner-reviewable proposals for a **new modern primer**, not fake translations of Spanda or Tantrasāra. Either the owner approves the explicitly labelled original prose contract, or the spec must revert to an extract-only reader with source-dependent slots. Mixing the two without disclosure would be a publication error.
'''
(P/'FULL_36_SPREAD_CANDIDATE_MANUSCRIPT.md').write_text(md)
(P/'candidate_36_spreads.json').write_text(json.dumps(records,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))
print('written',len(records))
